        "answer": {
          "short": "Line up the decimal points and compare digits from left to right. At the first difference, the larger digit identifies the larger number.",
          "worked": "Line up the decimal points. Compare the whole-number parts, then tenths, hundredths and subsequent places until the digits differ; add trailing zeros if helpful. The number with the larger digit at the first difference is larger. On a number line, it lies farther to the right.",
